    <!-- Synthetic (invented CVCV stems). The shapes HCLoader.cs writes for a project with
         NoDefaultCompounding=true and compound rules (LoadEndoCompoundingRule, LoadExoCompoundingRule):
         crE1 endocentric HeadLast=true (right member heads: headPartsOfSpeech is the right category, output
         copies nonhead then head); crE2 HeadLast=false; crE3 and crE4 the same with an OverridingMsa part of
         speech (outputPartOfSpeech="posR"). In FieldWorks every endocentric rule owns an OverridingMsa; where
         it has no part of speech (crE1, crE2) the rule has no outputPartOfSpeech, which is the "no override"
         shape. crX1 and crX2 are the two rules the loader emits for one exocentric rule (right head, then left
         head), both with the ToMsa part of speech; FieldWorks gives them the same name, here they differ because
         the harness cannot attribute a fired rule to a duplicated name. Stems K and L (demu, bonu) belong to a
         rule that is disabled in the project: the loader skips disabled rules, so the grammar has none.
         Suffixes are derivational affix rules (required and output part of speech); sufR and sufS name
         categories no stem has, so only a compound can take them. -->
    <PartsOfSpeech>
      <PartOfSpeech id="posA"><Name>leftA</Name></PartOfSpeech>
      <PartOfSpeech id="posB"><Name>rightB</Name></PartOfSpeech>
